 rise of platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, and Snapchat, young people are increasingly relying on social media to connect with others, express themselves, and consume information. However, the impact of social media on youth is a subject of debate among experts. One of the positive aspects of social media is that it allows young people to connect with others around the world. Platforms like Facebook and Instagram enable users to establish and maintain relationships, regardless of geographical boundaries. This can lead to increased social interaction and a sense of belonging, which is particularly important for youth who may feel isolated or disconnected. Moreover, social media provides a platform for young individuals to voice their opinions and raise awareness about social issues, empowering them to make a difference. On the other hand, there are concerns about the potential negative impact of social media on youth. One issue is cyberbullying, which has become increasingly prevalent on platforms such as Instagram and Snapchat. Cyberbullying can have detrimental effects on the mental health and well-being of young people, leading to anxiety, depression, and even suicide in extreme cases. Additionally, excessive use of social media can contribute to feelings of inadequacy and low self-esteem, as young people often compare themselves to others who seem to have perfect lives online. This can lead to a negative body image and a constant need for validation. Furthermore, social media can be a source of distraction for young individuals. With the constant need to check notifications and scroll through feeds, it can be difficult for youth to focus on their studies or engage in real-life activities. This can have a detrimental impact on academic performance and overall productivity. Moreover, excessive use of social media can lead to a sedentary lifestyle, as young people spend more time indoors on their devices instead of engaging in physical activities. In c